11
01:03:42,500 --> 01:03:48,500
Anora is a 2024 American romantic comedy-drama film written,
directed, produced, and edited by Sean Baker.

12
01:09:30,000 --> 01:09:36,000
It stars Mikey Madison as Anora "Ani" Mikheeva, a lap dancer from New York who
marries the wealthy son of a Russian oligarch played by Mark Eydelshteyn.

13
01:15:17,500 --> 01:15:23,500
The supporting cast includes Yura Borisov, Karren Karagulian, Vache
Tovmasyan, Darya Ekamasova, and Aleksei Serebryakov.

14
01:21:05,000 --> 01:21:11,000
Anora premiered at the 77th Cannes Film Festival on May 21, 2024, where
it received critical acclaim and won the Palme d'Or.

15
01:26:52,500 --> 01:26:58,500
It was released theatrically on October 18, 2024 by Neon.

16
01:32:40,000 --> 01:32:46,000
The film grossed $58.2 million worldwide against a $6 million
budget, making it Baker's highest-grossing film.

17
01:38:27,500 --> 01:38:33,500
Anora received numerous accolades.

18
01:44:15,000 --> 01:44:21,000
The film was named one of the top ten films of 2024 by the National
Board of Review and the American Film Institute.

19
01:50:02,500 --> 01:50:08,500
The film received six nominations at the 97th Academy Awards, winning five for Best Picture, Best
Director, Best Actress (Madison), Best Original Screenplay, and Best Film Editing.

20
01:55:50,000 --> 01:55:56,000
It is one of only four films to win both the Palme
d'Or and the Oscar for Best Picture.

21
02:01:37,500 --> 02:01:43,500
Anora also received seven nominations at the 78th British Academy Film Awards, winning two; five at the 82nd Golden Globe Awards; three at
the 31st Screen Actors Guild Awards; and one at the 70th David di Donatello for International Movie, which the film won.

22
02:07:25,000 --> 02:07:31,000
The film explores themes of new year's eve, new york
city, marriage, boardwalk, baptism.

23
02:13:12,500 --> 02:13:18,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
